cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "DSEM: Differentiable Spectral Element Method for PDE-constrained optimization"
abstract: >-
  DSEM embeds high-order Galerkin spectral element forward solves in the
  reverse-mode automatic differentiation engine of PyTorch, providing
  gradients for PDE-constrained inverse problems without deriving and
  maintaining problem-specific discrete adjoint implementations. It supports
  dense, sparse, and element-wise matrix-free evaluation modes and includes
  verification for linear elliptic and nonlinear steady residuals.
